.TH CHMAP_GET_ELEM_COPY 3 "2026-09-13" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chmap_get_elem_copy \- copy the value associated with a key out of a hash map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chashmap.h>

ccol_retval_t chmap_get_elem_copy(chmap chm, const cmap_pair *key_pair,
                                  void *target_buf, size_t target_buf_size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Searches the map for key_pair and copies the associated value into
target_buf, copying min(value_size, target_buf_size) bytes so an
undersized buffer receives a partial copy rather than an error. When
target_buf_size exceeds the stored value's size, the remaining bytes of
target_buf are zeroed rather than left untouched. cbmap_get_elem_copy(3)
takes the stricter approach of requiring an exact size match.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
chm              Hash map to search
key_pair         Key to look up
target_buf       Buffer to receive the value copy
target_buf_size  Size of target_buf
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - Key found, value copied into target_buf
ccol_key_not_found  - Key does not exist in map
ccol_invalid_args   - Any pointer is NULL, a size is 0, or key_pair's
                      size does not match a fixed-width key type's own
                      size (see chmap_create_full(3))
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(1) average complexity
Open-addressing: O(n) worst case for linear probing
Separate chaining: O(n) worst case per bucket, where n is chain length
Copies min(actual_value_size, target_buf_size) bytes
Safe to use with an undersized buffer, which receives a partial copy
Bytes of target_buf beyond the copied value are zeroed
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_get_elem_ref (3),
.BR chmap_insert_elem (3),
.BR cbmap_get_elem_copy (3)
